#: data/bridge.json
msgid "Beyond the Holy City the Kalinov Bridge crosses the Smorodina, the river of fire, from Nav to Yav, the living world, and every horde that comes walks over it. The volkhvs mean to raise it on from Yav to Prav, the realm of the gods: once the Ritual Arch joins it to Prav, the gods' light runs down the whole bridge and nothing from Nav can set foot on it again. The hordes know this, and will throw everything at the city on the night the arch is bound."
msgstr ""

#: data/bridge.json
msgid "Foundation Stones"
msgstr ""

#: data/bridge.json
msgid "Bring back a relic of the old builders from an ancient site: their mark, set in the first stone, binds the new span to the old bridge's end in Yav."
msgstr ""

#: data/bridge.json
msgid "A road to Prav can't rise from common stone. The old builders left their first stones among the ruins they abandoned, and only stones that remember the old rites will carry the bridge on from Yav."
msgstr ""

#: data/bridge.json
msgid "The Oak Piers"
msgstr ""

#: data/bridge.json
msgid "Clear a monster lair: the volkhvs won't raise an axe in the grove while the beasts are there."
msgstr ""

#: data/bridge.json
msgid "The piers that lift the bridge towards Prav are cut from the sacred oaks of the grove, but beasts of the North have made their lairs among the roots and nobody can fell a tree while they howl."
msgstr ""

#: data/bridge.json
msgid "The Iron Span"
msgstr ""

#: data/bridge.json
msgid "The forge is lit from the Holy City's own flame: weather a wave without the city losing Sanctity, or the flame gutters and the iron cracks."
msgstr ""

#: data/bridge.json
msgid "The ore comes through the passes: hold a pass or a fort on a horde's road, so the smiths know the road can be kept."
msgstr ""

#: data/bridge.json
msgid "Iron forged under Svarog's eye carries the road up into the sky. The forge must burn without break, fed by ore brought in through the passes."
msgstr ""

#: data/bridge.json
msgid "The Guardian Rails"
msgstr ""

#: data/bridge.json
msgid "The guardians' faces are copied from the old idols: bring back their likeness from an ancient site."
msgstr ""

#: data/bridge.json
msgid "A rail is quenched in the blood of a beast of the North: clear a lair to give the carvers what they need."
msgstr ""

#: data/bridge.json
msgid "The rails are carved with the faces of guardians so that nothing from Nav can climb the new span to Prav, and every rail must be quenched before it will hold."
msgstr ""

#: data/bridge.json
msgid "The Ritual Arch"
msgstr ""

#: data/bridge.json
msgid "Forge the ritual torc from a Svarog's Ember: the volkhvs bind the arch with it, and without it the new span is only a road into Prav for the enemy."
msgstr ""

#: data/bridge.json
msgid "The arch at the top of the span opens onto Prav. It is bound with a torc of Svarog's fire, and once it stands, everything in Nav will come at once: Ritual Night."
msgstr ""

#: data/bridge.json
msgid "Bring back a relic"
msgstr ""

#: data/bridge.json
msgid "Explore an ancient site while this stage is open."
msgstr ""

#: data/bridge.json
msgid "Clear a monster lair"
msgstr ""

#: data/bridge.json
msgid "An army clears a lair of the North while this stage is open."
msgstr ""

#: data/bridge.json
msgid "Weather a wave unscathed"
msgstr ""

#: data/bridge.json
msgid "A wave ends without the Holy City losing Sanctity since this stage began."
msgstr ""

#: data/bridge.json
msgid "Hold a strong point"
msgstr ""

#: data/bridge.json
msgid "Win a field battle at a choke point or from a fort while this stage is open."
msgstr ""

#: data/bridge.json
msgid "Craft the ritual torc"
msgstr ""

#: data/bridge.json
msgid "Forge the ritual torc from a Svarog's Ember."
msgstr ""

#: data/bridge.json
msgid "With the arch raised, the volkhvs begin the rite that will join the bridge to Prav. Every horde in Nav feels it. Tonight they all come at once, from every front, to break the city before the last words are spoken."
msgstr ""

#: data/bridge.json
msgid "The Kalinov Bridge holds"
msgstr ""

#: data/bridge.json
msgid "The last horde broke against the walls and the rite was finished. The Kalinov Bridge runs from Nav through Yav to Prav, the gods' light holds it end to end, the road from Nav is shut, and the bells of the Holy City ring for the first time in a generation. The old faith lives on, because you held."
msgstr ""

#: data/bridge.json
msgid "The Holy City has fallen"
msgstr ""

#: data/bridge.json
msgid "The walls are breached and the sanctuary fires are out. The hordes pour over the Kalinov Bridge unopposed. Some of the people escaped into the forests, carrying the songs with them; perhaps one day they will try again."
msgstr ""

#: data/buildings.json
msgid "Elder's Hall"
